{
  "requirement": "Ordinary evidence validation, status inspection, and book rendering MUST continue\nto check evidence using the existing rules without invoking models, contacting\nproviders, or requiring authoring configuration or credentials. Missing or stale\nevidence MUST remain a validation failure rather than trigger authoring.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment:** the implementation and tests satisfy the requirement. I found no gap.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Validation never authors or calls a model.** `inspect_repository_with_progress` (src/evidence.rs) is marked `{impl}`. Missing evidence is only pushed as an `evidence/<name>.json: missing for …` error (the comment says \"inspection never starts authoring\"). Stale evidence is reported by `validate_evidence_file`. Nothing in this path calls the `authoring::author_*` entry points. Those are only reached from `Command::Author` in src/main.rs.\n- **Workspace settings only.** `inspect_repository_with_progress` calls `config::load_workspace_evidence`, which reads only the workspace `[evidence]` rules. It does not decode `[authoring]` settings and does not resolve user configuration. The only authoring-related check is a scan for credential keys. It is marked `{impl}` and sits in src/config.rs. `UserConfig`, `resolve_authoring` and `load_user_config` are reachable only from the authoring path.\n- **Discovery needs no authoring configuration.** `DiscoverySources` and `DiscoverySources::load` (src/authoring/access.rs) read the Git index and the workspace evidence policy. They need neither authoring configuration nor Cargo metadata, and both are marked `{impl}`.\n- **Command dispatch.** `fn main` (src/main.rs) is marked `{impl}`. It runs `load_workspace_evidence` for the commands that resolve evidence inputs, skipping `status`, `info`, `setup`, `hook` and `mdbook supports`. `status` and `info` instead record an invalid workspace file as a validation finding. `mdbook` rendering calls `preprocess_book` and never touches authoring or credentials.\n- **No unspecified behaviour.** The marked code does not add behaviour beyond the requirement. The committed-credentials check is attributed to `requirements.authoring.credentials`, not to this requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- **`missing_or_stale_evidence_fails_validation_without_contacting_the_provider`** (tests/authoring_cli.rs).\n  - It covers both missing and stale evidence.\n  - For each case it asserts `validate_repository` reports the error.\n  - `status --all` and `mdbook` rendering both succeed with the model key removed from the environment.\n  - It checks that a listening provider socket receives no connection, that no usage state is written, and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n- **`ordinary_status_ignores_invalid_user_authoring_configuration`** (tests/authoring_cli.rs). `status` succeeds with a malformed user authoring configuration. It creates no state and does not change the evidence.\n- **Workspace-file tests** (tests/evidence_boundaries.rs, tests/commands.rs).\n  - Invalid common workspace configuration is reported as a finding.\n  - An invalid `[authoring]` section in `habeas.toml` is not validated or loaded (`validation_checks_workspace_common_config_without_loading_unused_authoring_settings`, `status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring`).\n  - A workspace disallow rule is still applied to evidence (`status_applies_workspace_disallow_to_existing_evidence`).\n- **Coverage of the design space.** The tests cover validation, status and book rendering, and the no-provider, no-credentials and no-authoring outcomes. The failure modes covered are missing evidence, stale evidence, and invalid authoring configuration. There are no acknowledged FIXMEs.",
  "references": "e3e78216d9f34ed3b581d36df93ac7b8c190716bc2e75723c09e3c2761be55b8",
